  "caption": "Quinn sprinted for the bus and felt a sharp twang in the back of the thigh. Two weeks on, jogging felt fine.\n\nPain-free jogging is a step, not the finish line. Rehab that includes trunk control, agility and loading the hamstring in lengthened positions tends to lower re-injury risk more than stretching alone.\n\nWhat can help: trunk and agility work early, slow lengthened loading later, return markers beyond pain (strength close to the other side and a pain-free single-leg hinge), and building sprints up gradually rather than relying on time alone.\n\nGet it checked if there was a pop with severe pain and you can't weight bear, bruising spreading towards the buttock, numbness or weakness, strong sitting-bone pain, or no change in 2–3 weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
